{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1121 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "76bb9e1b1605721b6f7070e5c0f595667f5891ee63a086b487bc80a174ee6664" :edb/db-before-t 1120 :edb/db-after-t 1121 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534433 50 #inst "2026-10-07T03:18:54.424Z" 13194139534433 true] [17592186064006 1100 "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int \\dfrac{1}{\\sin x}\\left(\\cot x + \\sin^2 x\\right)\\,\\textrm d x$." 13194139534433 false] [17592186064006 1100 "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int \\dfrac{1}{\\sin x}\\left(\\cot x + \\sin^2 x\\right)\\,\\textrm d x.$" 13194139534433 true] [17592186064006 1145 "We multiply out the parentheses and then use the identity\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{\\sin x} = \\csc x\n$$\n\nas follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int\\frac{1}{\\sin x}(\\cot x + \\sin^{2} x)dx &= \\int(\\frac{1}{\\sin x} \\cdot \\cot x + \\frac{1}{\\sin x} \\cdot \\sin^{2} x)dx \\\\\n&= \\int(\\csc x \\cdot \\cot x + \\sin x)dx \\\\\n&= \\int\\csc x\\cot xdx + \\int\\sin xdx \\\\\n&=-\\csc x - \\cos x + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534433 false] [17592186064006 1145 "We multiply out the parentheses and then use the identity $\\dfrac{1}{\\sin x } = \\csc x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}(\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\cdot \\operatorname{cot}⁡x+\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\cdot {sin}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{cot}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534433 true] [17592186064007 1100 "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int_0^{\\pi/3} \\dfrac{\\sin x}{\\cos^2 x}\\,\\textrm d x$." 13194139534433 false] [17592186064007 1100 "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int_0^{\\pi/3} \\dfrac{\\sin x}{\\cos^2 x}\\,\\textrm d x.$" 13194139534433 true] [17592186064007 1145 "We can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int_0^{\\pi/3} \\dfrac{\\sin x}{\\cos^2 x}\\,\\textrm d x =  \\int_0^{\\pi/3} \\dfrac{1}{\\cos x}\\cdot \\dfrac{\\sin x}{\\cos x}\\,\\textrm d x.\n$$\n\nWe then use the fact that $\\dfrac{\\sin x }{\\cos x}  = \\tan x$ and $\\dfrac{1}{\\cos x} = \\sec x$ to express this as\n\n$$\n\\int_0^{\\pi/3} \\sec x\\tan x\\,\\textrm d x,\n$$\n\nwhich is a standard trigonometric integral. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡x{|}_{0}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})-\\operatorname{sec}⁡(0) \\\\  & =2-1 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534433 true] [17592186064007 1145 "We can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int_0^{\\pi/3} \\dfrac{\\sin x}{\\cos^2 x}\\,\\textrm d x = \\int_0^{\\pi/3} \\dfrac{1}{\\cos x}\\cdot \\dfrac{\\sin x}{\\cos x}\\,\\textrm d x\n$$\n\nWe then use the fact that\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\sin x}{\\cos x} = \\tan x\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{\\cos x} = \\sec x\n$$\n\nto express this as\n\n$$\n\\int_0^{\\pi/3} \\sec x\\tan x\\,\\textrm d x\n$$\n\nwhich is a standard trigonometric integral. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int_{0}^{π/3}\\frac{\\sin x}{\\cos^{2} x}dx &= \\int_{0}^{π/3}\\sec x\\tan xdx \\\\\n&= \\left.\\sec x\\right|_{0}^{π/3} \\\\\n&= \\sec (\\frac{π}{3}) - \\sec (0) \\\\\n&= 2 - 1 \\\\\n&= 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534433 false] [17592186064008 1100 "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int \\tan{2x}\\,\\textrm d x$." 13194139534433 false] [17592186064008 1100 "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int \\tan{2x}\\,\\textrm d x.$" 13194139534433 true] [17592186064008 1145 "We use the identity\n\n$$\n\\tan 2x = \\dfrac{\\sin 2x}{\\cos 2x}\n$$\n\nand rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\tan{2x}\\,\\textrm d x = \\int \\dfrac{\\sin{2x}}{\\cos 2x}\\,\\textrm d x\n$$\n\nNotice that the numerator of the integrand is proportional to the derivative of the denominator. So, we can solve this by substitution.\n\nLet $u=\\cos 2x$. Then\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x}=-2 \\sin 2x \\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad -\\dfrac 1 2 \\,\\textrm d u= \\sin 2x \\, \\textrm d x\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int\\frac{\\sin 2x}{\\cos 2x}dx &= -\\frac{1}{2}\\int\\frac{1}{u}du \\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{2}\\ln\\begin{vmatrix}u & + C \\\\ =-\\frac{1}{2}\\ln & \\cos 2x\\end{vmatrix}+ C \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}\\ln\\begin{vmatrix}(\\cos 2x)^{-1} & + C \\\\ = \\frac{1}{2}\\ln & \\sec 2x\\end{vmatrix}+ C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534433 false] [17592186064008 1145 "We use the identity $\\tan 2x = \\dfrac{\\sin 2x}{\\cos 2x}$ and rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\tan{2x}\\,\\textrm d x = \\int \\dfrac{\\sin{2x}}{\\cos 2x}\\,\\textrm d x.\n$$\n\nNotice that the numerator of the integrand is proportional to the derivative of the denominator. So, we can solve this by substitution.\n\nLet $u=\\cos 2x.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x}=-2 \\sin 2x \\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad -\\dfrac 1 2 \\,\\textrm d u= \\sin 2x \\, \\textrm d x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x}\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x|+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)^{-1}|+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{sec}⁡2x|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534433 true] [17592186064137 1020 #edb/ref 17592186287977 13194139534433 true] [17592186064137 1020 #edb/ref 17592186287988 13194139534433 true] [17592186064137 1020 #edb/ref 17592186287991 13194139534433 true] [17592186064137 1020 #edb/ref 17592186287995 13194139534433 true] [17592186064137 1020 #edb/ref 17592186287998 13194139534433 true] [17592186064138 1020 #edb/ref 17592186288004 13194139534433 true] [17592186064138 1020 #edb/ref 17592186288008 13194139534433 true] [17592186064138 1020 #edb/ref 17592186288021 13194139534433 true] [17592186064138 1020 #edb/ref 17592186288028 13194139534433 true] [17592186064139 1020 #edb/ref 17592186287984 13194139534433 true] [17592186064139 1020 #edb/ref 17592186288001 13194139534433 true] [17592186064139 1020 #edb/ref 17592186288011 13194139534433 true] [17592186064139 1020 #edb/ref 17592186288014 13194139534433 true] [17592186064589 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534433 true] [17592186064589 1100 "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int\\tan x\\sqrt{\\cos x}dx$." 13194139534433 false] [17592186064589 1100 "Calculate $\\int \\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" 13194139534433 true] [17592186064589 1145 "We use the identity $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}$ and rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe can solve this by substitution. Let $u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,⟹\\,-\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}\\cdot (-\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =-\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}\\cdot \\text{d}u \\\\  & =-2\\sqrt{u}+C \\\\  & =-2\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534433 true] [17592186064775 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534433 true] [17592186064775 1100 "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int\\frac{\\tan^{2} x}{8\\sin^{2} x}dx$." 13194139534433 false] [17592186064775 1100 "Calculate $\\int \\frac{{tan}^{2}⁡x}{8{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" 13194139534433 true] [17592186064775 1145 "We can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{{tan}^{2}⁡x}{8{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{8}\\int {tan}^{2}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe then use the fact that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}$ and $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{tan}^{2}⁡x}{8{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{8}\\int {tan}^{2}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\int {(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x})}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\int \\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\int \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\int {(\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x})}^{2}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\int {sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534433 true] [17592186287977 1017 #edb/ref 17592186287978 13194139534433 true] [17592186287977 1089 "q-114304" 13194139534433 true] [17592186287977 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534433 true] [17592186287977 1100 "${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=$" 13194139534433 true] [17592186287977 1113 #uuid "a6e280b3-86c6-569b-92b8-e8e1faf4b4af" 13194139534433 true] [17592186287977 1145 "We use the identity $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =-(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡0) \\\\  & =-(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}-1) \\\\  & =1-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2-\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534433 true] [17592186287978 1000 #edb/ref 17592186287979 13194139534433 true] [17592186287978 1000 #edb/ref 17592186287980 13194139534433 true] [17592186287978 1000 #edb/ref 17592186287981 13194139534433 true] [17592186287978 1000 #edb/ref 17592186287982 13194139534433 true] [17592186287978 1000 #edb/ref 17592186287983 13194139534433 true] [17592186287978 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534433 true] [17592186287978 1041 "selection" 13194139534433 true] [17592186287978 1104 #edb/ref 17592186287979 13194139534433 true] [17592186287978 1110 #uuid "bc41b769-a9a6-5c26-8a8c-3056228d9575" 13194139534433 true] [17592186287979 1034 "\\frac{2-\\sqrt{2}}{2}" 13194139534433 true] [17592186287979 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534433 true] [17592186287979 1111 #uuid "f2cee3e9-f14d-5657-a811-73aba5a90c38" 13194139534433 true] [17592186287980 1034 "\\sqrt{2}+2" 13194139534433 true] [17592186287980 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534433 true] [17592186287980 1111 #uuid "ab8971bf-232f-54d5-a114-5e925701fd1a" 13194139534433 true] [17592186287981 1034 "\\frac{1-\\sqrt{2}}{2}" 13194139534433 true] [17592186287981 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534433 true] [17592186287981 1111 #uuid "b6458493-786c-5814-bbb7-25c682d059ba" 13194139534433 true] [17592186287982 1034 "2(\\sqrt{2}-1)" 13194139534433 true] [17592186287982 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534433 true] [17592186287982 1111 #uuid "299f4206-9551-573b-9992-27f2e505639a" 13194139534433 true] [17592186287983 1034 "1-\\sqrt{2}" 13194139534433 true] [17592186287983 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534433 true] [17592186287983 1111 #uuid "2ea198b6-6c7a-5099-b6be-a3de0252f133" 13194139534433 true] [17592186287984 1017 #edb/ref 17592186287985 13194139534433 true] [17592186287984 1089 "q-347941" 13194139534433 true] [17592186287984 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534433 true] [17592186287984 1100 "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\pi /9}^{\\pi /6}\\frac{3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{{sin}^{2}⁡(3x)}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534433 true] [17592186287984 1113 #uuid "7ea22259-6d5c-5d45-907a-d0498167099b" 13194139534433 true] [17592186287984 1145 "We can solve this by substitution. Let $u=\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x.$ Then \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNow, we fill the table for the limits of integration, according to the rule $u=\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x.$\n\n| $x$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{9}$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$ | $1$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /9}^{\\pi /6}\\frac{3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{{sin}^{2}⁡(3x)}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\sqrt{3}/2}^{1}\\frac{1}{{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{u}{|}_{\\sqrt{3}/2}^{1} \\\\  & =-(\\frac{1}{1}-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}-1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534433 true] [17592186287985 1000 #edb/ref 17592186287986 13194139534433 true] [17592186287985 1000 #edb/ref 17592186287987 13194139534433 true] [17592186287985 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534433 true] [17592186287985 1041 "field-1" 13194139534433 true] [17592186287985 1104 #edb/ref 17592186287987 13194139534433 true] [17592186287985 1110 #uuid "0c9be182-5976-5eb0-9dec-4b6aa38d35d3" 13194139534433 true] [17592186287986 